<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hurrians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hurrian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hurrians were a people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">ancient Near East</a>, speaking a language unrelated to Semitic or Indo-European tongues, who were widespread in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. They formed the main population of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni Empire</a>, ruled by an Indo-Aryan elite. Hurrian religion and culture also strongly influenced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>.</p></div>
